{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1473836-concepts-for-river-cities","id":1473836,"title":"Concepts for River Cities","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Geist: The Sin-Eaters"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-02-02T10:07:31-08:00","id":1473836,"title":"Concepts for River Cities","content":"Hello everyone!<br /> So I'm storytelling a Geist Chronicle set in my hometown of Natal (Brazil) during the second world war when it had an american flying base for USA's war planes, and there was a large influx of american culture and people here, and while I have a good grip on the living side of the setting, I fell like I'm not very inspired for describiing a River City with an unique flavor<br /> <br /> This led me to realize that, in general, I struggle with flavoring my River Cities with anything beyond debris shantytowns and favelas. the best I could manage was flavoring and describing a river city which was created based on a fallen Monastery occupied by very religious ghosts, but I feel like these cities can be so much more than that.<br /> <br /> Considering all that I'm starting this thread hoping everyone could drop some cool ideas for unique and interisting River Cities, its customs, its inhabitants, its architecture, and so on!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25516-pinkhaunt","name":"PinkHaunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T11:16:42-08:00","id":1473843,"title":"","content":"Not all that familiar with Geist (more of a Requiem player &amp; ST), but considering the <a href=\"https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forte_dos_Reis_Magos\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Forte dos Reis Magos</i></a> was pretty much one of the first permanent structures built in the area, even before the city came to be, after defeating the french and their native allies and has seen its share of battles and use as political prison through the centuries, giving it an Underworld reflection seems like a non-issue, at least to me.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/Forte_dos_Reis_Magos.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">quite scenic</a> to boot.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would suggest certain parts of a river city could reflect major eras or threshold events of the city's history, with some local folklore and <a href=\"https://todonatalense.com.br/natal/as-9-maiores-lendas-urbanas-que-ja-existiram-em-natal/\" target=\"_blank\">urban legends</a> mixed in for extra strangeness. <a href=\"https://curiozzzo.com/os-7-super-mitos-de-natal-rn/\" target=\"_blank\">Samples</a> to look into and tinker with can definitely be found online.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T11:32:06-08:00","id":1473846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Baaldam</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1473836-concepts-for-river-cities?p=1473843#post1473843\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not all that familiar with Geist (more of a Requiem player &amp; ST), but considering the <a href=\"https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forte_dos_Reis_Magos\" target=\"_blank\"><i>Forte dos Reis Magos</i></a> was pretty much one of the first permanent structures built in the area, even before the city came to be, after defeating the french and their native allies and has seen its share of battles and use as political prison through the centuries, giving it an Underworld reflection seems like a non-issue, at least to me.<br /> <br /> Not to mention, <a href=\"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/f/f7/Forte_dos_Reis_Magos.jpg\" target=\"_blank\">quite scenic</a> to boot.<br /> <br /> <br /> I would suggest certain parts of a river city could reflect major eras or threshold events of the city's history, with some local folklore and <a href=\"https://todonatalense.com.br/natal/as-9-maiores-lendas-urbanas-que-ja-existiram-em-natal/\" target=\"_blank\">urban legends</a> mixed in for extra strangeness. <a href=\"https://curiozzzo.com/os-7-super-mitos-de-natal-rn/\" target=\"_blank\">Samples</a> to look into and tinker with can definitely be found online.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, amazing points, thank you for your considerations and for taking the time to look up a bit of Natal's history in order to answer, that is very much appretiated!<br /> <br /> Will be using your tips and suggestions on my story thank you!!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25516-pinkhaunt","name":"PinkHaunt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25516_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"27"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-02T12:00:44-08:00","id":1473848,"title":"","content":"You're welcome. Also, in a little bit of a crossover note, you might want to look into the <i>Kanaima </i>from Skinchangers, south american jaguar spirits with themes of justice, vengeance and watching over the dead, who not only will at times respond to proper prayers and offerings to help a person seek revenge, but <i>they\u2019ll animate dead bodies to seek out revenge on their killers in order to fuel the dead\u2019s (and their own) hunger for revenge</i>.<br /> <br /> Great fodder for games involving the dead, risen or not, native american legendry (in brazil and a number of neighboring countries both) and things that may blur &amp; cross the line between ghost, vampire/zombie, werebeast, dark vengence-fueled ritual magic and more depending on how one plays up with the parts.<br /> <br /> (In fact in a 1e Requiem chronicle i played the &quot;Gangrel&quot; was truly a combatant from the <a href=\"https://pt.wikipedia.org/wiki/Revolu%C3%A7%C3%A3o_Federalista\" target=\"_blank\">Revolu\u00e7\u00e3o Federalista</a> brought back as a ravenous dead through a deal of his witch lover with one of the kanaima and had some peculiar features related to interacting with ghosts - represented by supernatural merits - because of it)<br /> <br /> <br /> Truth be told, between Anhang\u00e1s (independent ghoul families of nebulous native american origin with a talent for Protean), Kanaima (filling a bit the niche of the Strix and <i>maybe</i> also connected to the Anhang\u00e1s), Sightless Mother, Red Jack, Reapers (from Mythologies, possibly Kerberoi but we never delved seriously on this), Mnemovores, larvae (think zombies on speed) hordes commanded by a Morbus apocalyptic cult, Melissidae connnected to Phanariot (from Mythologies) &amp; Abyssal Spiders (from Intruders: Encounters with the Abyss), not to mention the &quot;Nonatii/Neverborn&quot; (pre-human ur-vampires, connected to the Blood Gods from Mythologies, modeled with some critters from Predators) in the Land of Worms - the version of Rio de Janeiro the PCs interacted with could be quite the freak circus even without the vampires. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 02-02-2022, 03:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-07-24T08:36:20-07:00","id":1487732,"title":"","content":"Southeast Asian river-boat culture could fit perfectly.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}